  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, due to its excessive cumulative depth and a mix of eaves and roof heights, has created an incongruous and unsympathetic 'add-on' structure on the rear elevation that fails to integrate well within the context and detracts from the appearance of the existing dwelling, the pair of semi-detached houses, the 'Bute Road Estate' Area of Special Local Character and the street scene. As such, the proposal is contrary to policy 28 and 30 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and the guidance as set out within SPD 4 'Design of Residential Extensions'.\r",
    "The proposal, by reason of its excessive depth on the shared boundary with No. 53 Bute Road and its proximity to the shared boundary with 2 Eastway, has resulted in a dominant form of development that has caused loss of outlook from the rear gardens and the first floor windows of these adjacent properties, contrary to policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its fenestration positioned above the shared boundary fence and the proximity of this fenestration facing directly the rear primary windows and rear garden of No. 2 Eastway, has resulted in an undue impact on the occupiers of this adjacent property in terms of perceived sense of overlooking and sense of enclosure, contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
